<ContentPage title="Privacy policy" description="This policy explains what happens when you use zyvento and our online word counter." eyebrow="Legal">
  <section><h2>What this website does</h2><p>zyvento currently provides a browser-based word counter. The core counting process runs on your device. Text entered into the counter is not sent to a server to calculate the results, put into the URL, or saved in local storage by the tool.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>You can use the word counter without an account or signup. If you contact us by email, we receive the information you choose to include, such as your email address, message, and attachments, and use it to respond.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Preferences and technical information</h2><p>The site stores your light or dark theme preference in your browser’s local storage if you change the theme. Your writing is not stored there. Like most websites, the hosting environment may process ordinary technical request information such as an IP address, browser, and time of request to deliver and protect the site. We do not use the word counter to log or analyze the text you enter.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Third parties</h2><p>The current tool does not use a third-party text-processing API or analytics script. If this changes, this policy will be updated before or when the new service is introduced, along with any relevant choices available to you.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Children and policy changes</h2><p>The service is a general-purpose utility and is not directed at collecting information from children. We may update this policy as the site develops. The “Last updated” date above shows when the current version was published.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:hello@zyventowordcouter.com">hello@zyventowordcouter.com</a>.</p></section>
</ContentPage>
